    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0506" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/492: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-29T19:00:00+08:00">November 29, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 29—7:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1056. Your 394, November 28, noon. Following from American Consul in charge at
                    Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 28, 4 p.m. Reliably informed that Tsai Yun-sheng arrived at
                            Mukden from Vladivostok on the 26th with Soviet terms for the holding of
                            a [conference?] and restoration of power of Soviet manager and immediate
                            release of prisoners.</p>
                        <p>After conference of high officials at Marshal’s<anchor n="33"
                                xml:id="d284-f1"/> villa same day a telegram was sent to Moscow
                            accepting in principle Soviet terms on <pb facs="0507" n="363"
                                xml:id="pg363"/> condition that terms 1 and 3 be first referred to a
                            joint committee to arrange procedure. Old wing of party<anchor n="34"
                                xml:id="d284-f2"/> responsible for this peace overture. No reply as
                            yet.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d284-f1" n="33" xml:id="d284-f1-content">
